  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x200b;&#x200b;Rapid Stabilization Support to Somalia (RSS)&#x200b;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Spontaneous community-led uprisings against al-Shabaab (AS) gained momentum in the second half of 2022, galvanizing government efforts to exert greater control over newly recovered territory of Somalia. Urgent stabilization support is needed to consolidate the gains made by the Somali population over the extremist network and to bolster responsible civilian governance in target locations. The proposed project harnesses the experience of IOM in delivering stabilization support to newly liberated and fragile areas of Somalia, which is optimized by a dynamic combination of local embeddedness, interdisciplinary expertise, and operational depth. The objective is to contribute to stability and peace through an integrated stabilization package that provides a bridge to longer-term development interventions, with an exit strategy defined in conjunction with government and civil society counterparts.</narrative>
  </description>
